      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-116621",
      ":question/problem": "The following table shows the number of customers per minute, $c(t),$ that arrive at a shop counter over a period of $120$ minutes.\n\n| $t\\,(\\text{minutes})$ | $0$ | $30$ | $80$ | $120$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $c(t)\\,(\\text{customers/minute})$ | $10$ | $8$ | $6$ | $12$ |\n\nUse the trapezoidal rule with the partition\n\n$$\n[0,30]\\cup [30,80]\\cup [80,120],\n$$\n\nto approximate the total number of customers served in two hours."
